The input provided is already in a structured JSON format. However, if you want to format it in the specified manner, here's how you can do it using Python:

```python
import json

input_data = '''
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "mint",
            "vulnerability": "Mint for Zero Address",
            "correctness": 9,
            "severity": 7,
            "profitability": 5,
            "criticism": "The mint function in this smart contract is vulnerable to mint for zero address. An attacker can bypass the presale address condition to mint tokens for free. This makes the mint function highly profitable for attacker."
        }
    ]
}
'''

# Parse the input data into a Python object
json_data = json.loads(input_data)

# Format the JSON data as per the specified format
formatted_data = {
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": json_data["output_list"][0]["function_name"],
            "vulnerability": json_data["output_list"][0]["vulnerability"],
            "criticism": json_data["output_list"][0]["criticism"],
            "correctness": json_data["output_list"][0]["correctness"],
            "severity": json_data["output_list"][0]["severity"],
            "profitability": json_data["output_list"][0]["profitability"]
        }
    ]
}

# Print the formatted JSON data
print(json.dumps(formatted_data, indent=4))
```

The output of this program will be:

```json
